# life.pdl - needs, death, respawn and drops of this game (owner 2026-10-25). Re-read every 2 s, no rebuild.
# LIFE | key | value | what it does
LIFE | enabled      | 0        | 1 = hunger, death, respawn and life bars on; 0 = off (the default in a game that has just got the life layer)
LIFE | hunger_ms    | 60000    | ms for hunger to rise by 1 (0..100); at 100 each step costs starve_hp
LIFE | starve_hp    | 1        | hp lost per hunger step once hunger is 100
LIFE | drop_pct     | 50       | percent of every item stack that falls where they died (0 = keep all, 100 = drop all)
LIFE | death_mode   | respawn  | respawn = back on the safe place with full hp; permadeath = stays dead for good; session = stays dead until `life reset` / the next session
LIFE | respawn_room | bridge   | the safe place: room id ...
LIFE | respawn_x    | 7        | ... and cell
LIFE | respawn_y    | 5        |
LIFE | take_range   | 2        | how many cells away a drop can be taken from (anyone can take)

# ACTOR | id | position file (in state/) | max hp   the characters the world-ops steps (events/death, events/respawn: wo kv / drop / place) work on; the skin reads only the LIFE rows.
# The hero is a state file of its own (trainer.txt), every pal has pet_<id>.txt. Max hp = what `life status` shows as the second number.
ACTOR | harold  | trainer.txt      | 450
ACTOR | ember   | pet_ember.txt    | 20
ACTOR | glacine | pet_glacine.txt  | 20
ACTOR | murmur  | pet_murmur.txt   | 20
ACTOR | solvent | pet_solvent.txt  | 20
